rstanding of my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T21:19:07-08:00","id":1438682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1028971-pre-divine-war-map?p=1438555#post1438555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can find quite a bit in the old (3.X) Scarred Lands Campaign Setting: Ghelspad (not the Gazeeter, the 200+ pages book)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Random aside: would anyone know why Darakeene and Hollowfaust figure in Zathiske's list of &quot;enemy nations&quot; in the book? It bugs the hell out of me because it seems to be something unique to it, unlike Burok Torn &amp; Durrover that figure as common enemies of all calastian-dominated nations, and yet i can't seem to find any straight explanation for it. Hollowfaust in particular still figures as such in later editions, still with no explanation (though i'd guess it relates to the necromancers' settling on Sumara, once a celebrated zathiskan city before the Divine War).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avata